  "name": "Yu opera (Henan bangzi)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Yu opera Henan provincial Chinese opera tradition, the largest of the bangzi (wooden-clapper) opera family by audience and the second-largest Chinese opera tradition after jingju by aggregate national reach. Origin in seventeenth-eighteenth century Henan from earlier folk-music synthesis with qinqiang influences. Distinguished from neighboring qinqiang by softer, more lyrical vocal register and accessible Henan-dialect Mandarin language. Canonical play Hua Mulan (the female-warrior legend) constitutes the type-specimen of yu opera's strong female-protagonist tradition. The post-1949 Henan Yu Opera Theatre under Chang Xiangyu consolidated the modern repertoire.",
